# Assign-to-Content-Project UI (canonical)

Assign to Content Project has exactly one canonical **right-side** workspace/sidebar.
All callers use the shared opener and shared backend.
No caller-specific modal/drawer/form is allowed.

Before implementing assignment of any article, keyword, SEO issue, anchor, internal link, vocabulary planning item, or future content entity to a Content Project:

MUST reuse:
- Blade trigger `x-content::assign-to-content-project-trigger`
- Filament `AssignToContentProjectActionFactory`
- React `assignToContentProject.js` opener (`openAssignToContentProject`)
- open event `assign-content-project:open` (`AssignToContentProjectContract::OPEN_EVENT`)
- Livewire `AssignToContentProjectDrawer` + view `content::livewire.assign-to-content-project-drawer`
  (right-side: `inset-y-0 right-0`, not left, not centered modal)

MUST NOT introduce:
- a second assign drawer
- an assign modal (centered or Filament) as the user-facing UI
- a left-side assign drawer
- a new Filament assign form/schema on Actions
- a new React/Alpine assign form
- a new assign-specific event name
- a new visual trigger pattern (icon/color/label)
- caller-specific assign forms/schemas

Canonical ownership (source of truth):
- Contract + ActionFactory → `content-projects`
- Drawer class + Blade view + Blade trigger + React opener → `content`
- `seo-content-ai-compat` may mount/consume only — never own a parallel assign UI

Compatibility notes:
- `AssignToContentProjectModal` / `assign-to-content-project-modal` may exist only as aliases that
  delegate to the same Drawer implementation — they must not render a second UI.

Domain differences use modes (`article` | `keyword` | `pending_link` | `vocabulary_items`) and context/options.
`source` must not select backend business logic.

Laravel-only articles (`wp_post_id` null) must remain assignable — assignment must not require WordPress.

If unsupported: extend the canonical contract/component and its tests/docs.
Do not create a parallel implementation.
